//
// BOUNDS and each entry's `d` path share the same projection that
// map-geometry.ts uses to place structure pins: longitude maps linearly onto
// x in 0..800, and latitude maps linearly onto y in 0..MAP_HEIGHT. MAP_HEIGHT
// is not 800. One degree of longitude is about 2.5% shorter than one degree
// of latitude at this latitude (cos 12.8 degrees), and BOUNDS spans 0.66
// degrees of latitude against 0.80 of longitude, so keeping the real shape
// means the box is 800 wide and about 675 tall. An earlier version squeezed
// both ranges into 800 x 800, which stretched the province north to south by
// about 19%. Keep BOUNDS, MAP_HEIGHT and the paths in step: if one changes,
// regenerate the paths from the source data with the same math, do not
// hand-edit them, or pins and boundaries drift apart.
